Animation: count a track's keys within the length without searching when they all are.

_interpolate() ran _find(keys, length) on every call, a second binary search per
track per frame, only to count the keys at or before the animation's end. When the
last key is within the length, which is the usual case, that's every key. The
search now runs only when the last key is past the end.

Upstream: not proposed yet. Drop when an equivalent change is in the Godot we pin.

